WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.167
Joining us now

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:04.804
perhaps the most FULL-THROATED critic,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.141
the former president has on this subject

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.542
among his Republican

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.510
primary opponents, former

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.478
New Jersey Governor Chris

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.380
Christie, who, of course, I should remind

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.014
everyone will be

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.315
joining Anderson

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.416
Monday night

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.051
for a CNN town hall, which

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.220
I will be eagerly watching

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:20.854
Governor Christie,

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:21.888
thanks so much for joining us

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.423
and popping in to give you a reaction

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.724
on this important day.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:25.291
Last night

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.926
you said no one's above the law,

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:27.861
but you wanted to wait

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.962
and read the indictment

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.330
before reacting which,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.064
you know, frankly,

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.632
seems like a responsible thing to do.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.733
Now you've read it.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.868
What do you think

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.204
Oh, Jake, look,

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.539
you know, for the folks

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.740
who may not remember this,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.643
I did this for seven years as U.S.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.078
attorney in New Jersey,

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.312
the fifth largest U.S.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.013
attorney's office

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.681
out of the 93 in the country

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.616
bought 130

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.684
political corruption prosecutions

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.053
against Republicans and Democrats

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.187
and didn't lose one.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.156
So I know how this stuff works.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.390
And the fact is that

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.360
these these facts are are devastating.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.063
You know, you have a president who,

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.497
according to the indictment,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.499
directed the packing of those boxes

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.535
in terms of what to take, directed

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.502
where they should go tomorrow.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.538
Largo directed where they went while

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:12.972
they were inside Mar a Lago,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.842
directed them to move to Bedminster

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.377
during the summer

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.244
when he would spend

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.413
his summers in New Jersey.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.116
And and then when requests came,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.118
starting in May of 2021

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.853
informal requests,

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.822
he continued to stonewall them

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.291
and not return the documents.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.326
Then when a subpoena came,

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.762
asks his lawyers, Jake,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.429
whether or not

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.730
we even have to respond to it.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.732
We have to play ball,

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:40.166
you know,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.367
and then

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.570
try to get them to lie on his behalf.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.537
And when they

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:44.971
when he knew

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:45.572
they wouldn't

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.206
and his own lawyer

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.508
had to make recordings to protect himself

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.009
when either they wouldn't,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.912
he directed his folks to hide boxes

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.447
from his own lawyer

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:54.881
in order

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.149
not to turn these documents

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.751
over to the government.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.786
Look, you know,

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:00.820
people are going to argue about

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.321
who should

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.323
and who should not have been indicted

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.791
and who should be tried.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.292
But let me say this.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.328
The bigger issue for our country is,

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.296
is this the type of conduct

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.097
that we want

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.031
from someone

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.366
who wants to be president

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.168
of the United States?

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.704
To take national security documents

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.940
involving warfare and our nuclear program

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.776
to keep them in their in their home

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.578
when they're not allowed to do so,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.580
exposing them to a potential bully

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.315
being seen by any number of people

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.818
and then actually showing them to people

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.752
showing off.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.389
This is irresponsible conduct.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.291
And look at the time

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.226
when Hillary Clinton was not charged.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.594
I argued against that.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.929
I think she should have been charged.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.531
I think that was a mistake.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.633
And during the Russia investigation,

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:47.867
I was one of the people who spoke out

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.168
and said,

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.002
I don't think Donald Trump

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.003
anything to do with it.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.771
I was involved with the campaign

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.872
and I didn't think there was anything

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.140
to the Russian collusion

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.409
as it applied to Donald Trump.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.278
So I spoken out against those things

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.579
when I think they were wrong.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.447
But just because they were wrong

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.348
doesn't justify

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.350
the conduct that he engaged in.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.351
And I think we have to focus

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.686
on the conduct, Jake.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:09.088
And the conduct is bad

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.125
and it is bad for anybody in this country

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:12.692
to do it.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.093
But it's particularly awful

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.129
for someone who has been president

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.097
and who aspires to be president again.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.465
So as a former U.S.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.600
attorney,

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.102
does this look like a case that you would

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.504
theoretically have brought

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.471
had you been assigned

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:28.208
You know, I don't know

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:28.942
all the facts, Jake,

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:29.642
but I'll tell you this.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.710
It's a very,

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.179
very evidence filled indictment.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.314
What you can tell,

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.349
there's a trained person reading this is

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.551
they have tape recordings.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.519
They have electronic

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.287
text messages and emails,

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.989
and they have the testimony

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.992
of dozens of people who were right around

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.427
Donald Trump in Mar-A-Lago

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.295
and in Bedminster over time.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.463
Those are all the elements

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:50.997
of the things

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.433
you need to bring a case like this.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.001
And so what I would say

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.136
is that it looks like these prosecutors

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.037
and their partners

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.873
at the FBI thoroughly investigated this.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.543
And it looks like the only two people

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.278
who did not cooperate

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.279
with the government

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.881
are Donald Trump and not.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.949
And I think that's why

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.251
they're on the wrong side of the V,

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.585
as we say in the business

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.754
and have been charged in this case,

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.490
Republican officials, whether candidates

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.892
or elected officials,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.361
seem to be falling into into

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.729
three groups. One is

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.465
those who are just being quiet

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:27.000
that's most of them.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.034
Then there is those

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.670
who are vociferously defending

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.972
Donald Trump.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.008
And then there's a small group of you

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:35.942
and the governor, Asa

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.478
Hutchinson, and Mitt Romney.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.912
Adam Kinzinger.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:40.847
This afternoon, House

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.181
Speaker McCarthy said that

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.317
this indictment will disrupt the nation.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.787
He says that it calls into question

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.622
equal justice for all.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.290
Congressman Andy

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.291
Biggs

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.592
says that we've reached

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.061
a, quote, warfare phase.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.430
What do you make of the rhetoric?

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:59.232
And what do you make of the fact

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.100
that you and

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:01.601
you in such

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.669
a small group of people

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.603
willing to call out

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.872
this alleged lawlessness?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.909
I think the group will get larger,

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:10.610
Jake,

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.978
as everyone gets an opportunity

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.680
to absorb the facts.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.248
Look, I agree

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.283
with Speaker McCarthy in this respect.

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:19.352
The indictment will disrupt the nation.

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.020
But let me ask you a question.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.056
Who's responsible for that?

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:23.890
The conduct

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.991
that Donald Trump engaged

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.026
in was completely self-inflicted

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.463
in May or June or July

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.498
or August of 20, 21.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.567
He could have just returned

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.302
the documents.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:36.903
And in fact,

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.538
if you look at the indictment,

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.640
even the documents that he did return

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:44.811
is subject to the subpoena in 20, 20 to

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.813
those documents.

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.681
He wasn't charged on any of them.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.683
So even if he had given all the documents

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.352
back in response to the subpoena

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.320
as he was legally required to do,

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.988
we wouldn't be here today.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.023
So everyone wants to blame

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:57.757
the prosecutors.

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:58.524
And look,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.227
I think the prosecution, DOJ is at fault

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:03.096
for not charging Hillary Clinton.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:04.831
It's at fault for what happened

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.466
in the Russia investigation

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.601
because it undercut people's

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.770
faith and confidence in the system.

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.672
But each case has to be

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.374
looked at on its own merits.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.476
And the facts that are laid out here

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.344
are damning in terms

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.546
of Donald Trump's conduct.

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.316
And that's what I think we as a party

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:24.450
should be looking at.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.319
Do we really believe that someone

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.521
who engaged in this type of conduct

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:30.623
is going to be the best person

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.759
to put up against Joe Biden?

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.726
That's the question.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.161
We should be asking.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.262
Congress has the ability

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.430
to have oversight

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.731
over the Department of Justice,

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.533
and I encourage them to do it

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.101
vigorously and fairly

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.202
and ask all the questions

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.971
they need to ask of the leadership

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.272
of the Department of Justice.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.774
That's what we should be doing.

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.642
But what we should also be doing

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.777
is holding to account

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:52.445
people who are in positions

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:53.913
of responsibility

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.480
and saying,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.982
if you act badly,

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.084
there has to be penalties for that.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.319
There has to be a cost to be paid.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.722
And he could have avoided all of this

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:05.458
if he had just returned the documents

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:06.626
at any point,

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:07.326
if he hadn't taken them

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.194
in the first place.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:09.595
But once he took them,

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:10.997
if he had returned them at any time

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.965
between January of 20, 21

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.301
and August of 20, 22,

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.502
he wouldn't be here tonight

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.070
and the country wouldn't be here.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.139
He has contributed mightily

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.707
to subjecting the country

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:22.241
to the pain

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:23.443
that we're going to go through

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:24.010
over the course

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.578
of the next number of months because

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:26.446
of what's going on.

